<title>NETHERLANDS: Fedex FDX N meets union in bid to stop dispute.</title>
<headline>Fedex FDX N meets union in bid to stop dispute.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. integrator Federal Express will meet FNV union members on Friday to try to prevent further strike action in the Netherlands, a FNV spokesman said.</p>
<p>Members of FNV, the largest Dutch union, went on strike at several FedEx branches on Wednesday in a dispute over a new salary system that had been introduced.</p>
<p>Strike action has been postponed pending the outcome of the meeting which is expected to take place on Friday at 1500 GMT.</p>
<p>The express operator employs 150 people in the Netherlands.</p>
